<h1>NearestSpot Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="updated">Last updated: July 29, 2026</p>

<h2>1. Overview</h2>
<p>NearestSpot ("the app") shows interesting places near you. The app has no backend servers, requires no account, and collects no personal data.</p>

<h2>2. Location</h2>
<p>To find nearby places the app requests access to the device's location (precise or approximate) only while the app is in use. Coordinates are used solely to make anonymous requests to public open APIs: Wikipedia/Wikimedia, OpenStreetMap Overpass API, Baidu Baike, and Openverse. Coordinates are never stored or shared with any other third party.</p>

<h2>3. On-device data</h2>
<p>Saved places and settings are stored locally on your device only and are never transmitted anywhere. Uninstalling the app removes this data completely.</p>

<h2>4. Navigation apps</h2>
<p>Only upon your explicit action ("Route" button) the app passes destination coordinates to external navigation apps (Yandex Maps, Google Maps, 2GIS, Amap, Baidu Maps), which process data under their own policies.</p>

<h2>5. Analytics and ads</h2>
<p>The app contains no analytics SDKs, trackers, or advertising modules.</p>

<h2>6. Children</h2>
<p>The app is not directed at children and does not knowingly collect children's data.</p>

<h2>7. Changes</h2>
<p>The current version of this policy is always available on this page.</p>

<h2>8. Contact</h2>
<p>Privacy questions: <a href="https://github.com/fireresistance/nearest_spot/issues">github.com/fireresistance/nearest_spot/issues</a></p>
